{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the sons of Kehat: Amram and Yitzhar and Chevron and Uzziel — for three sons of Kehat: Amram, Yitzhar, and Uzziel, he specifies their children. But for Chevron he does not specify. And if you will say: because he had no children — but is it not written in the census of Pikudim: ״ומשפחת החברוני״? And why did he not specify here the children of Chevron? Because their names are not mentioned in the Torah before us, but these three — Amram, Yitzhar, and Uzziel — their children were mentioned in the Torah. Amram's, on account of Aharon and Moshe and Miriam. The children of Yitzhar, on account of Korah, as it is written: ״ויקח קרח בן יצהר וגו׳״. The children of Uzziel, on account of Mishael and Elitzafan, as it is written: ״ויקרא משה וגו׳ ואל אליצפן בני עוזיאל דוד אהרן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The lemma's names follow standard transliteration. Rashbam's closing quotation 'ואל אליצפן בני עוזיאל דוד אהרן' follows the Hebrew text as he cites it (compare Leviticus 10:4)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:36.027015367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}